## Why
The linker needs an entry point and cannot find a function named `main` (`undefined reference to 'main'` in `_start`). The source compiled fine; it simply defines no `main`, or its name is misspelled (for example `Main`).
## Fix
Add a `main` function that calls your code.
```cpp
int main() {
    // call your code here
    return 0;
}
```

